Part M - Offering the Role to the Preferred Candidate
(57)
Under no circumstances is a “conditional” offer of employment to be made. All elements of the selection process must be completed prior to any job offer.
(58)
A verbal offer can be made by the TA team member or the Hiring Manager, at which time they should confirm:
the specific position, title, and salary grade;
the direct reporting relationship;
remuneration (including any consideration for gender pay gap);
an appropriate starting date;
Probationary period
Probation periods are set in accordance with the relevant probation policy and in accordance with the
Enterprise Agreement
.
Campus location
Supervisor
Time fraction (part-time/fractional only)
Relocation assistance (if applicable)
Visa assistance (if applicable)
Salary loading (if applicable) and duration]
Willingness to undertake a Victorian Employee Working with Children Check (Refer to
Working with Children Policy
)
Confirm if any workplace adjustments are required
Proof of work rights in Australia
In order to be employed by the University, all applicants are legally required to have what is referred to as ‘the right to work” or equivalent in Australia;
It is the University’s responsibility to ensure that every person hired is legally eligible to work in Australia;
If the applicant indicates they are Australian or from New Zealand, they must provide a copy of their passport, birth certificate or Australian Citizenship Certificate;
Where a non-Australian or non-New Zealand citizen has applied for a role, a copy of their residency status is required including a copy of the relevant visa providing this entitlement to work and any restrictions relevant;
If the applicant required University sponsorship (refer to
Visa Sponsorship Policy
).
Academic Qualification Check
Copies of transcripts of educational qualifications, including degrees, diplomas or certificates that are relevant to the role must be obtained from the new staff member. For example, an applicant applying for a qualified accountant or legal role.
